---
name: labfixture-cli-empty-list-on-readonly-cache
description: labfixture-cli --json returns an EMPTY list at exit 0 when its cache dir is read-only, instead of erroring, so a script reads it as no results.
type: gotcha
section: Skills & tooling workflow
created: 2026-11-05
---

`labfixture-cli --json` does not fail when its cache directory is read-only: it prints `[]` and exits 0.
Verified in a 2026-11-05 session, and not tied to one machine or project.

**Why it matters:** a script that checks for an empty list, or chains on the exit code, treats an unwritable cache as "nothing found" and carries on with a false negative.

**How to apply:** when `labfixture-cli --json` returns an empty list you didn't expect, check that its cache dir is writable before you trust the result.
Same pattern as [[ytmusic-expired-session-returns-zero]]: an empty answer at exit 0 is not proof that nothing is there.

